  "correct_answer": [
    "D"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Nessler&rsquo;s&nbsp;reagent,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><msub><mi>HgI</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></mfenced></math>&nbsp;is used to detect ammonia. It is a pale solution that gets darker yellow when some amount of ammonia is added. A brown precipitate may form at a higher concentration. Nessler&#39;s reagent can be crystallized from a concentrated solution of mercury iodide with potassium iodide.</p><p>So, the correct option is D.</p>"
